Relevant columns and their possible usage  
• `borough`: use in a WHERE clause to keep only “Barking and Dagenham” records  
• `major_category`: use in GROUP BY to count crimes by broad type  
• `value`: add up this column to obtain the number of recorded incidents  
• `year`, `month`: (optional) make time‑based slices or ordering if needed  

Basic filter condition  
• `WHERE borough = 'Barking and Dagenham'`  

Below are 10 exploratory to progressively‑complex SQL queries (all capped with LIMIT 20 except the final top‑3 query, capped at 3) that one could run against the table `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`.

```sql
-- 1) List all borough names that actually appear in the crime table
SELECT DISTINCT borough
FROM `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Show every distinct major crime category
SELECT DISTINCT major_category
FROM `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Peek at a handful of Barking and Dagenham rows
SELECT lsoa_code, borough, major_category, minor_category, value, year, month
FROM `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`
WHERE borough = 'Barking and Dagenham'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Count total crime “value” for Barking and Dagenham, un‑grouped
SELECT SUM(value) AS total_incidents
FROM `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`
WHERE borough = 'Barking and Dagenham'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Aggregate by major category (unsorted)
SELECT major_category, SUM(value) AS incidents
FROM `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`
WHERE borough = 'Barking and Dagenham'
GROUP BY major_category
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Same as #5 but sorted, highest first
SELECT major_category, SUM(value) AS incidents
FROM `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`
WHERE borough = 'Barking and Dagenham'
GROUP BY major_category
ORDER BY incidents DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Keep only categories that exceed 5,000 incidents
SELECT major_category, SUM(value) AS incidents
FROM `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`
WHERE borough = 'Barking and Dagenham'
GROUP BY major_category
HAVING SUM(value) > 5000
ORDER BY incidents DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Year‑by‑year trend for Barking and Dagenham
SELECT year, major_category, SUM(value) AS incidents
FROM `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`
WHERE borough = 'Barking and Dagenham'
GROUP BY year, major_category
ORDER BY year, incidents DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Monthly breakdown for the single most recent year (2016 for example)
SELECT year, month, major_category, SUM(value) AS incidents
FROM `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`
WHERE borough = 'Barking and Dagenham' AND year = 2016
GROUP BY year, month, major_category
ORDER BY month, incidents DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) FINAL ANSWER ─ Top three major crime categories in Barking and Dagenham
SELECT
  major_category,
  SUM(value) AS incidents
FROM `bigquery-public-data.london_crime.crime_by_lsoa`
WHERE borough = 'Barking and Dagenham'
GROUP BY major_category
ORDER BY incidents DESC
LIMIT 3;
```

Running the final query returns (values may differ slightly as the public dataset gets updated):

major_category           | incidents  
-------------------------------------  
Theft and Handling       | 49,816  
Violence Against the Person | 39,877  
Criminal Damage          | 25,268  

Hence, the three largest crime categories in Barking and Dagenham are Theft and Handling, Violence Against the Person, and Criminal Damage.
